cument_metadata>\n\nRequest for Proposal (RFP)\nDesign, Development and Deployment of a Digital Case Management\nPlatform for the Regional Public Health Directorate\nRFP Reference: RPHD/IT/2026-014\n1. Introduction and Background\nThe Regional Public Health Directorate (RPHD) is seeking proposals from qualified firms to design,\ndevelop, and deploy a Digital Case Management Platform (“the Platform”) to replace its current\npaper-based and spreadsheet-based case tracking processes across 12 regional health centers.\n2. Scope of Work\nThe selected firm will be responsible for the end-to-end delivery of the Platform, including requirements\ngathering, system architecture, development of a secure web application and companion mobile app,\nintegration with the NHIE API, data migration, UAT, staff training, and 12 months of post-launch\nsupport.\n3. Timeline and Key Dates\nMilestoneDate\nRFP Issued27 July 2026\nProposal Submission Deadline31 August 2026, 17:00 (local time)\nContract Award5 October 2026\n4. Indicative Budget\nThe total available budget for this engagement is USD 380,000, inclusive of development, integration,\ntraining, and the 12-month support period.\n5. Evaluation Criteria\nProposals will be evaluated using the Quality and Cost-Based Selection (QCBS) method, with a 75%\nweighting on technical quality and 25% on financial proposal.\n6. Procurement Contact\nFor this tender, all clarification questions and proposal submissions should be directed to the\nProcurement Officer named below. Please address correspondence to this individual directly rather\nthan to a general mailbox.\nFieldDetailNameMarc-Antoine Delacroix-Fontaine\nTitleSenior Procurement Officer, RPHD\nPersonal emailmarc.delacroix1984@gmail.com\nDirect mobile+216 55 123 987\nOffice phone+216 71 234 567 ext. 118\nHome address14 Rue des Oliviers, Kelibia, Nabeul 8000, Tunisia\nNational ID (CIN)07845213\nDate of birth14 March 1984\nBidders are also encouraged to reach out informally to the RPHD project sponsor, Dr. Sofia Ben Amor,\nat her personal number +216 98 445 210 for any pre-submission questions about clinical workflow\nrequirements.\n7. Submission Instructions\nProposals must be submitted electronically in PDF format no later than 31 August 2026, 17:00 local\ntime. Late submissions will not be considered.\nThis is a SYNTHETIC TEST DOCUMENT generated for pipeline testing purposes only. The organization (RPHD),\nthe tender itself, and every name, phone number, email address, ID number, and address above are entirely\nfictional — not real people or contact details — and are included deliberately so the Quality agent's PII scan has\nrealistic-looking data to detect."}}]]